  "# ADR-2607198200: Add kagi and kagitaba to stack security enforcement

## Context

The first stack score omitted `kotoba-lang/kagi` and `kotoba-lang/kagitaba`.
That omission understated the stack: kagi already executes hybrid
X25519+ML-KEM-768 wrapping, hybrid Ed25519+ML-DSA-65 signatures, native
non-exportable signing and decapsulation handles, key lifecycle, threshold
recovery, witnessed rotation and deployment-readiness attestations. Kagitaba is
not a vault; it is the pure item/import boundary consumed by kagi.

## Decision

The score register covers eight repositories. Kagi owns secret custody,
hybrid-PQC, key lifecycle and governed reveal. Kagitaba owns lossless but
bounded admission and sensitivity classification. Kagitaba must never acquire
crypto or persistence responsibility.

Kagi's Governor now evaluates subject, resource, action and environment:
identity/role/tenant/clearance, item tenant/classification, operation, purpose,
device trust, network zone, validity window and disclosure size. Once a policy
declares a condition, a missing attribute denies. Decisions expose the policy
id and evaluated attributes for the audit receipt.

The 1PUX file boundary now limits entry count, name length, per-entry expanded
bytes and total expanded bytes. Absolute paths, traversal segments,
backslashes, NUL names and duplicate entries fail closed before JSON parsing or
attachment materialization. These are decompressed-byte limits, not compressed
metadata hints, so a false ZIP size cannot bypass them.

## Qualification boundary

Software can require HTTPS, verify signed checkpoints and reject replay or
split-view evidence, but a cross-machine confidentiality claim requires a real
mTLS endpoint, certificate rotation and downgrade test. Software can produce
containment/revocation/recovery plans, but a closed-loop operations claim needs
immutable remote telemetry, deployed isolation authority, independent clean
backup and measured RTO/RPO. Those remain deployment attestations and cannot be
marked complete by local unit tests."}]
